# A held callable is called by the formals of the header of its declared type.
# A name that is none of them is refused as it is for a method: the actual
# under it is taken by place, and the formal named after it is given twice.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
h2: make2 100
int: r h2(z: 2; x: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
